---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import RelocationLeadForm from "../../components/relocation/RelocationLeadForm.astro";
import { site } from "../../config/site";

const phoneHref = site.contact.phone.replace(/[^\d+]/g, "");

const pageSchema = [
  {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://ajtayfel.com/relocation/chicago-to-southwest-florida/#webpage",
    url: "https://ajtayfel.com/relocation/chicago-to-southwest-florida/",
    name: "Moving From Chicago to Southwest Florida",
    description:
      "A homeowner-focused relocation hub for coordinating an Illinois home sale with a move to Southwest Florida.",
    about: {
      "@id": "https://ajtayfel.com/#aj-tayfel"
    }
  },
  {
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: 1,
        name: "Home",
        item: "https://ajtayfel.com/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: 2,
        name: "Relocation",
        item: "https://ajtayfel.com/relocation/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: 3,
        name: "Chicago to Southwest Florida",
        item: "https://ajtayfel.com/relocation/chicago-to-southwest-florida/"
      }
    ]
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Moving From Chicago to Southwest Florida | AJ Tayfel"
  description="A homeowner-focused guide to selling in Illinois and planning a move to Fort Myers, Cape Coral, Naples, Estero, Bonita Springs, and Southwest Florida."
  schema={pageSchema}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Illinois → Southwest Florida</p>

        <h1>
          Selling in Illinois.<br />
          Moving to Southwest Florida.
        </h1>

        <p class="hero-lede">
          Plan your Illinois home sale and Florida move as one coordinated
          transition — with local representation here and an introduction to
          an appropriately licensed real estate professional at your
          destination.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button-premium primary" href="#relocation-form-heading">
            Start My Relocation Plan
          </a>

          <a class="text-link" href="#destinations">
            Explore Southwest Florida
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <p class="hero-disclosure">
          Illinois real estate services provided by AJ Tayfel. Florida
          representation, when needed, is provided by appropriately licensed
          Florida real estate professionals.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-index" aria-label="Southwest Florida destinations">
        <p class="index-label">Southwest Florida</p>

        <div class="index-destinations">
          <span>Fort Myers</span>
          <span>Cape Coral</span>
          <span>Naples</span>
          <span>Bonita Springs</span>
          <span>Estero</span>
        </div>

        <div class="index-footer">
          <span>From Chicagoland</span>
          <span>To the Gulf Coast</span>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how-it-works" class="process-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A Coordinated Approach</p>
          <h2>One move. Two markets. One plan.</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          An interstate move becomes easier to manage when the Illinois sale
          and Florida purchase are planned around the same timeline instead
          of treated as unrelated transactions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="process-grid">
        <article class="process-step">
          <span class="step-number">01</span>
          <h3>Prepare the Illinois side</h3>
          <p>
            Review your home, preparation needs, listing strategy, likely
            timing, and what the sale needs to accomplish before the move.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="process-step">
          <span class="step-number">02</span>
          <h3>Define the Florida move</h3>
          <p>
            Clarify the communities, property type, timing, budget, and
            ownership questions that matter at your destination.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="process-step">
          <span class="step-number">03</span>
          <h3>Connect both sides</h3>
          <p>
            When destination representation is needed, I can coordinate an
            introduction so both sides understand the larger relocation plan.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="destinations" class="destinations-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Explore Southwest Florida</p>

        <h2>
          Start narrowing the place that feels right.
        </h2>

        <p>
          You do not need to know exactly where you want to live before
          starting. Begin with the places that deserve a closer look, then
          refine the search around your lifestyle, property preferences,
          budget, and ownership priorities.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="destination-features">
        <a
          class="destination-feature"
          href="/relocation/chicago-to-fort-myers/"
        >
          <div class="destination-top">
            <span class="destination-number">01</span>
            <span class="destination-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="destination-type">Relocation Guide</p>
            <h3>Fort Myers</h3>
            <p>
              A central Southwest Florida option with a broad mix of housing
              types and access to surrounding Gulf Coast communities.
            </p>
          </div>

          <span class="destination-link">Explore Fort Myers</span>
        </a>

        <a
          class="destination-feature"
          href="/relocation/chicago-to-cape-coral/"
        >
          <div class="destination-top">
            <span class="destination-number">02</span>
            <span class="destination-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="destination-type">Relocation Guide</p>
            <h3>Cape Coral</h3>
            <p>
              A large waterfront-oriented community where flood, insurance,
              utilities, and property-specific due diligence deserve careful
              attention.
            </p>
          </div>

          <span class="destination-link">Explore Cape Coral</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="destination-index">
        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>Naples</strong>
          <p>Collier County living, condominiums, communities, and luxury options.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>Bonita Springs</strong>
          <p>A location between Fort Myers and Naples with access to both regions.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <strong>Estero</strong>
          <p>Planned communities, newer development, and regional convenience.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <strong>Still deciding?</strong>
          <p>That is completely fine. Destination planning can begin before the city is final.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="agent-section">
    <div class="container agent-grid">
      <div class="agent-image-wrap">
        <img
          src="/images/aj-headshot.png"
          alt="AJ Tayfel, REALTOR®"
          class="agent-image"
          width="900"
          height="1125"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="agent-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Your Illinois-Side Point of Coordination</p>

        <h2>
          Meet AJ.
        </h2>

        <p class="agent-lede">
          Relocation works better when somebody keeps the entire move in view.
        </p>

        <p>
          I help homeowners plan and handle the Illinois real estate side of
          the transition — including preparation, listing strategy, timing,
          and communication around the sale.
        </p>

        <p>
          When you need representation in Florida, I can help identify and
          introduce you to an appropriately licensed real estate professional
          based on the market and type of help you need.
        </p>

        <div class="agent-services">
          <div>
            <span>01</span>
            <strong>Illinois home-sale strategy</strong>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>02</span>
            <strong>Relocation timeline coordination</strong>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>03</span>
            <strong>Destination-agent introduction</strong>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="agent-actions">
          <a class="button-premium dark" href="#relocation-form-heading">
            Plan My Move
          </a>

          <a class="direct-link" href={`tel:${phoneHref}`}>
            Call {site.contact.phone}
          </a>

          <a class="direct-link" href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>
            Email AJ
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guides-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Relocation Planning Guides</p>
          <h2>Make the big decisions before they become urgent.</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          These guides focus on the homeowner questions that often determine
          how an Illinois-to-Florida move should be sequenced.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="guide-grid">
        <a
          class="guide-card"
          href="/relocation/selling-illinois-home-before-moving-to-florida/"
        >
          <span class="guide-number">01</span>

          <div>
            <p class="guide-label">Home Sale Planning</p>

            <h3>
              Selling Your Illinois Home Before Moving to Florida
            </h3>

            <p>
              Think through preparation, listing timing, closing coordination,
              and how the Illinois sale fits into the move.
            </p>
          </div>

          <span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>

        <a
          class="guide-card"
          href="/relocation/should-you-sell-illinois-house-before-buying-in-florida/"
        >
          <span class="guide-number">02</span>

          <div>
            <p class="guide-label">Transaction Sequence</p>

            <h3>
              Should You Sell Your Illinois House Before Buying in Florida?
            </h3>

            <p>
              Compare selling first, buying first, and coordinating both
              transactions during an interstate move.
            </p>
          </div>

          <span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="questions-section">
    <div class="container questions-grid">
      <div class="questions-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Before You List</p>

        <h2>
          A few questions can shape the entire move.
        </h2>

        <p>
          There is no universal sequence. The right plan depends on your
          property, financing, timing, flexibility, and destination.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="decision-list">
        <div class="decision">
          <span>01</span>
          <p>
            Do you need proceeds from the Illinois sale before purchasing
            in Florida?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <span>02</span>
          <p>
            Would you rather sell first, buy first, or coordinate both
            transactions closely together?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <span>03</span>
          <p>
            How much flexibility do you have if one closing happens before
            the other?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <span>04</span>
          <p>
            Have you researched Florida-specific ownership questions such as
            insurance, associations, and property-specific flood considerations?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <span>05</span>
          <p>
            Are you already represented by a real estate professional in
            either market?
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container planning-note">
      <p>
        These are planning prompts only and are not financial, legal, tax,
        insurance, or lending advice. Appropriate professionals should be
        consulted for those areas.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section">
    <div class="container faq-grid">
      <div class="faq-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</p>

        <h2>
          Chicago to Southwest Florida relocation.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>
            Should I sell my Illinois home before buying in Florida?
          </summary>

          <p>
            There is no single sequence that works for everyone. Your
            available equity, financing, desired timing, housing flexibility,
            and comfort with carrying two properties can all affect the
            decision. The important part is planning both transactions early.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            Can you help me buy a home in Florida?
          </summary>

          <p>
            My role is on the Illinois side of the move. When Florida
            representation is needed, I can help connect you with an
            appropriately licensed Florida real estate professional.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            What if I do not know which Southwest Florida city I want?
          </summary>

          <p>
            You can still begin planning. Your housing priorities, budget,
            timing, lifestyle preferences, and ownership requirements can help
            determine which communities deserve further investigation.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            How early should I start planning an interstate move?
          </summary>

          <p>
            Earlier planning generally provides more flexibility. Even if the
            move is six to twelve months away, it can be useful to begin
            discussing the Illinois property, destination requirements, and
            possible transaction sequence.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            What if I already have a Florida agent?
          </summary>

          <p>
            That is fine. The relocation form lets you indicate whether you
            already have representation so the Illinois side can be planned
            without duplicating an existing relationship.
          </p>
        </details>

        <p class="license-note">
          Florida real estate services are provided by appropriately licensed
          Florida real estate professionals when applicable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing-cta">
    <div class="container closing-inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow light">Ready When You Are</p>

        <h2>
          Start with the move you are actually trying to make.
        </h2>

        <p>
          Tell me about your Illinois home, your timing, and where you are
          considering going. We can begin from there.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="button-premium light-button" href="#relocation-form-heading">
        Start My Relocation Plan
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <RelocationLeadForm />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(html) {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  .hero,
  .process-section,
  .destinations-section,
  .agent-section,
  .guides-section,
  .questions-section,
  .faq-section,
  .closing-cta {
    --ink: #102c3c;
    --ink-deep: #092432;
    --paper: #fbfaf6;
    --warm: #f2eee6;
    --line: rgba(16, 44, 60, .16);
    --gold: #a88b55;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: .72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hero {
    min-height: 720px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem) 0;
    background: var(--paper);
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.08fr) minmax(330px, .72fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-copy h1,
  .section-heading h2,
  .agent-copy h2,
  .questions-heading h2,
  .faq-heading h2,
  .closing-cta h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .hero-copy h1 {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(3.6rem, 7.5vw, 7rem);
    line-height: .96;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
  }

  .hero-lede {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    color: #4d5d65;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.22rem);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.25rem 2rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .button-premium {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 52px;
    padding: .9rem 1.6rem;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform .2s ease,
      background .2s ease,
      border-color .2s ease;
  }

  .button-premium:hover,
  .button-premium:focus-visible {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .button-premium.primary,
  .button-premium.dark {
    background: var(--ink-deep);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .text-link,
  .direct-link {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: .25em;
  }

  .text-link span {
    margin-left: .45rem;
  }

  .hero-disclosure {
    max-width: 690px;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: #78838a;
    font-size: .78rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .hero-index {
    min-height: 540px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    background: var(--ink-deep);
    color: white;
  }

  .index-label,
  .index-footer {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.55);
    font-size: .7rem;
    letter-spacing: .16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .index-destinations {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .index-destinations span {
    padding: .8rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.15);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.7rem);
  }

  .index-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .process-section {
    padding: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem) 0;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .section-heading {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .section-heading h2,
  .agent-copy h2,
  .questions-heading h2,
  .faq-heading h2,
  .closing-cta h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 5vw, 4.7rem);
    line-height: 1.03;
    letter-spacing: -.03em;
  }

  .section-heading > p:not(.eyebrow),
  .split-heading > p {
    color: #647078;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .split-heading {
    max-width: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr .75fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    align-items: end;
  }

  .process-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .process-step {
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .step-number,
  .destination-number,
  .guide-number,
  .decision span,
  .agent-services span {
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: .72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .13em;
  }

  .process-step h3 {
    margin: 1.3rem 0 .8rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 1.65rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .process-step p {
    color: #647078;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .destinations-section {
    padding: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem) 0;
    background: var(--warm);
  }

  .destination-features {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: rgba(16,44,60,.18);
    border: 1px solid rgba(16,44,60,.18);
  }

  .destination-feature {
    min-height: 470px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    background: var(--paper);
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background .25s ease;
  }

  .destination-feature:hover,
  .destination-feature:focus-visible {
    background: #fff;
  }

  .destination-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .destination-arrow {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    transition: transform .2s ease;
  }

  .destination-feature:hover .destination-arrow {
    transform: translate(3px, -3px);
  }

  .destination-type,
  .guide-label {
    margin-bottom: .65rem;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: .72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .destination-feature h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .destination-feature p:not(.destination-type) {
    max-width: 480px;
    color: #647078;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .destination-link {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: .25em;
  }

  .destination-index {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    margin-top: 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .destination-index > div {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .destination-index > div + div {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .destination-index span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: .75rem;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: .7rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .destination-index strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .destination-index p {
    margin-top: .65rem;
    color: #647078;
    font-size: .88rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .agent-section {
    padding: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem) 0;
    background: var(--ink-deep);
    color: white;
  }

  .agent-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 410px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .agent-image-wrap {
    width: 360px;
    justify-self: center;
    padding: 10px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.16);
  }

  .agent-image {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .agent-copy .eyebrow {
    color: #c7ad79;
  }

  .agent-copy h2 {
    color: white;
  }

  .agent-lede {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 1.7rem 0 1rem;
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .agent-copy > p:not(.eyebrow):not(.agent-lede) {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.72);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .agent-services {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);
  }

  .agent-services > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 55px 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
